Changelog: 09-10-2026 13:56:58

install.sh also puts an icon on the Desktop; --no-desktop-shortcut leaves it out, and --uninstall removes
it. Options can now be combined, e.g. --run --no-desktop-shortcut.

Changelog: 08-10-2026 04:17:40

Designed a new icon.
Changelog got another look.

Changelog: 07-10-2026 12:59:27

The interface is now translatable and ships in nine languages: English, German, Spanish, French, Italian, Polish,
Russian, Simplified Chinese and Japanese (303 strings each, including the whole Help page and the
backend status/error messages). The language follows the system locale; the Help page has a picker that is saved
and applied at the next start, and `--lang CODE` overrides it for one run. Qt's own dialog buttons are translated
via the qtbase catalogs. New tooling: `tools/update_translations.sh` (pylupdate6 extraction) and
`tools/compile_translations.py`, a pure-Python .ts to .qm compiler so no release is needed; the release workflow
recompiles the .qm files. Tests check every shipped translation for completeness, preserved placeholders and a
loadable .qm, and that switching the language actually changes the UI text.

Changelog: 07-10-2026 12:21:16

Deploy: the Steam library box no longer jumps back to "pick a game" after Scan or a library rescan
(the lookup compared Path objects by identity). Setup: answering No to "Download and build again?" now says so on the
page instead of doing nothing silently. Tooltips are parented to the window they belong to, which stops Wayland's
"Failed to create popup" messages on every hover.

Changelog: 07-10-2026 11:59:56

New Setup page: one click downloads the latest HelixSR release, parses the URLs and SHA-256 sums its setup scripts pin,
fetches NVIDIA's DLSS DLL, Microsoft's DXC and (on read-only systems) the portable Python in parallel with checksum
verification, runs `helixsr-setup.sh --yes` with its output streamed to the page, deletes the DLSS DLL and imports
the built release as the payload. A DLSS 310.7.0 DLL already on the PC can be used instead (*Find in Steam* compares
checksums). Update checks for the HelixSR payload and for this app against GitHub's latest releases, at start
(switchable) and on demand, with a hint on the Overview when a newer HelixSR exists.
New CLI flags `--work DIR` and `--no-update-check`. Help and README describe the flow; 15 new tests run the whole
setup against a fake script over `file://`.

Changelog: 07-10-2026 07:18:40

Rewrite of the app around how HelixSR actually works. 
HelixSR replaces a game's `amd_fidelityfx_upscaler_dx12.dll` / `amd_fidelityfx_dx12.dll` 
(kept as `*.original.dll`) and needs its two network files next to it; 
the previous version treated it as an nvngx/dxgi injector with DLSS presets and launch options, 
none of which apply. New: payload import from the extracted release or zip (network files are never shipped), 
Steam library discovery, DLL scan with per-file status, replace mode and stand-alone OptiScaler 
folder mode with the `OptiScaler.ini` snippet, reversible remove, a deployment list with live state, 
a full `helixsr.ini` editor that keeps the upstream comments, and a Help page. 
Packaging fixed: working `install.sh` (keeps the payload on uninstall), desktop entry, icon, GitHub workflows for 
tests and releases, and a pytest suite. Layout, widgets and installer mirror bc250-governor-manager.
